cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "osiris-mobile-termux: an Android/Termux research harness, and a negative result for evolved parameterized quantum circuits as byte-level language models"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it. Negative results are part of the record."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Davis
    given-names: Devin Phillip
    email: osiris.dnalang@gmail.com
    affiliation: Agile Defense Systems LLC
version: 0.4.0-edge-beta
date-released: 2026-09-22
license-url: "https://github.com/osiris-dnalang/osiris-mobile-termux/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: https://github.com/osiris-dnalang/osiris-mobile-termux
abstract: >-
  Execution harness running the OSIRIS research stack entirely on Android under
  Termux: a tiered installer whose default compiles nothing but NumPy (dnalang
  imports qiskit lazily, so the artificial-life and compiler front-end track needs
  no Rust build), a fold-aware tmux layout that migrates running panes as the device
  hinge opens, a hysteretic battery and thermal governor, deterministic intent
  routing that separates explaining a subsystem from running it, and a ladder runner
  that will stage but never launch an experiment whose criterion is not already
  committed. Two pre-registered experiments are included with their data. LivLM-PPL-1
  met its criterion (median held-out byte perplexity 125.26 vs uniform 256.0, 5/5
  seeds) and is recorded PASS, with a diagnostic showing the criterion was confounded
  by a decoder smoothing term - the circuit's own distribution is about 70x worse
  than uniform. LivLM-PPL-2, the missing control, finds evolved 72-angle genomes
  worse than random genomes on 5/5 seeds (median ratio 1.401): FAIL, branch closed.
  No hardware; no physical claim.
keywords:
  - edge computing
  - Termux
  - parameterized quantum circuits
  - language models
  - pre-registration
  - negative results
